# Task 5: Matrix Algebra and Matrix Operations

## 1. Objective

The aim is to use matrices in Python to rotate and resize a square.

## 2. Inputs

The program uses four points that form a square. It rotates the square by 45 degrees, makes it twice as wide, and increases its height by 1.5 times.

## 3. Mathematical Operations

The program uses matrices to change the positions of the square's corners. It combines a rotation matrix and a scaling matrix to calculate the new coordinates.

## 4. Original Output

The program displays the original points, the transformation matrix, the new points, and the determinant.

The determinant is approximately 3.

## 5. Modified Input

I changed the rotation angle from 45 degrees to 90 degrees.

## 6. Observation

Changing the angle changes the positions of the square's corners. The square is still rotated and resized, but its final position and orientation are different.

## 7. Interpretation

Matrices make it easier to rotate and resize objects by calculating their new coordinates. This is useful in computer graphics and animation.

## 8. Related Real-World Problem

A computer game needs to rotate and resize an object on the screen. The program can use matrices to calculate the new positions of the object's corners.

## 9. Assumptions

The object is represented by four points. The program uses a rotation angle of 90 degrees and keeps the same scaling values.

## 10. New Input Data

The rotation angle is changed from 45 degrees to 90 degrees. The scaling values remain 2.0 for width and 1.5 for height.

## 11. Output

The program produces new coordinates for the four corners of the square.

## 12. Interpretation of the Modified Problem

The new coordinates show the changed position of the object after rotation and resizing. This method can help computer games and graphics programs move and change objects on the screen.